# Security overrides for vulnerable transitive BUILD tooling.
#
# Scope: dependencies of the build itself (Gradle plugins and the libraries they
# drag in), not dependencies of the shipped application. Application
# dependencies are declared in gradle/libs.versions.toml and updated there.
#
# Why this file exists: when an advisory affects a transitive build dependency,
# the fix is usually a forced version rather than a plugin upgrade, and that
# force must be auditable. Putting it here keeps the reason, the advisory and
# the removal condition next to the version, instead of burying a resolution
# strategy in build.gradle.kts.
#
# Format — one override per line:
#
#   <group>:<artifact> = <version>  # <advisory-id> <reason> (remove when <condition>)
#
# Lines starting with '#' are comments; blank lines are ignored. The root build
# script reads this file and applies each entry to the buildscript classpath.
#
# Rules:
#   * Every entry cites the advisory it answers.
#   * Every entry states the condition under which it must be removed, so that
#     overrides do not outlive the vulnerability.
#   * Entries are reviewed whenever the Android Gradle plugin or Kotlin version
#     changes, because an upgrade frequently makes an override obsolete.
#
# There are no overrides at present.
